I switched over to refinement list from hierarchicalMenu but they both have the sortBy attribute. 
You could create a numeric  attribute to sort by and use for sorting. 

Here is some code: 

` S.addWidget(instantsearch.widgets.refinementList({
            container: "#search-facet-categories",
            attributeName: "MyAttribute",
            sortBy: ["AttributeToSortBy:desc"],
            operator: "or",
            limit: 100,
            autoHideContainer: true,
            templates: {
                header: "Review Value",
               },            },
            cssClasses: {
                active: "selected"
            },
            transformData: function(e) {
                return e
            }
        }));`

ohh, I see, i try another way using 
sortBy: function(a, b) {
      return -1;
    },
so the first (choosen) will show the first.
but i have another  problem now, is there any whay to hide the first parent in hierarchicalMenu ?
I try 
showParentLevel: false, 
but it just hide the second and else parent, but the first will always show up.
